  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "Keys L and Keys R (AES50-A 15/16) are sequential, named as an L/R pair, and are not overheads, so merged into one stereo channel 'Keys' per the conventions' sequential-stereo-pair rule; source.input records the first socket's row name (Keys L) as the stereo channel reference point, per domain convention for pairing.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "OH (AES50-A 17) is a single mic with no L/R designation in its name, so there is no pairing decision to make here; it stands as one mono overhead channel.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bass has no dedicated DCA named in the conventions' DCA list (Drums/Guitars/Keys/Vocals/Tracks/Strings/Horns), so BassDI joins the 'Band' DCA under the rule 'Include all other instruments not included in one of the DCAs above'.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "No 'Strings' DCA or mix bus was created: the input list has no strings-category channels, and the conventions only create these groups 'if there is at least one member' / 'if there are multiple strings'.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "No 'Keys' mix bus was created: the conventions require 'multiple keyboards' to trigger it, and this show has a single (stereo) keyboard instrument.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "Channels BassDI, EG 1, Keys, and TRAX are not members of any mix bus, so they are routed straight to Main via main_routes to satisfy 'every input needs an output'. They still carry DCA membership (Band/Guitars/Keys/Tracks) per the DCA rules; per domain knowledge a DCA creates no signal path, so DCA membership does not substitute for, or preclude, this direct main routing.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "Monitor bus convention states sends should be left 'all the way down, mute off, PRE fader'. The bus_sends schema in this format has only level_db and mode (no per-send mute flag), so the 'mute off' instruction is only represented by leaving mute off at the fader/global level; it is not separately encoded on the send itself.",
      "source": "model"
